                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0767230e-6a59-3225-89d1-84250c3022ad",
                                        "entry_id": "8113bd45-ce91-3af7-8c28-a2eaaf16da85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Latin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ddbfb45-7255-4057-be62-5edfe71dac61",
                                                "sense_id": "0767230e-6a59-3225-89d1-84250c3022ad",
                                                "text": "\"And your name?\" she said, \"I suppose it's quite unremarkable?\" \"Very funny.\" \"Mark. It could stand as a symbol of a man, for men as a category,\" she reflected, \"but I don't suppose that's why your mother gave it to you?\" \"My mother's motives always were impenetrable to me. I was her only child, she wanted a simple life. So she gave me a simple name to go along with it. --- It wasn't a popular name until the nineteenth century. People were put off by King Mark in the Tristram and Iseult.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94b312db-0611-45a4-826b-1eb57d26d84e",
                                                "sense_id": "0767230e-6a59-3225-89d1-84250c3022ad",
                                                "text": "One Nation, a new 501(c)4 linked to the Karl-Rove-backed American Crossroads super PAC, is spending more than $1.9 million on print, radio and digital ads highlighting the efforts of Illinois Sen. Mark Kirk, North Carolina Sen. Richard Burr, New Hampshire Sen. Kelly Ayotte, Ohio Sen. Rob Portman and Pennsylvania Sen. Pat Toomey to pass the “doc fix” legislation that realigned payments to Medicare providers with inflation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dd9a83f-9f24-3408-8125-a081bc200a08",
                                        "entry_id": "8113bd45-ce91-3af7-8c28-a2eaaf16da85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c666eb0-672e-3138-85af-ec75cb8ecf52",
                                        "entry_id": "8113bd45-ce91-3af7-8c28-a2eaaf16da85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mark the Evangelist, also called John Mark, the first patriarch of Alexandria, credited with the authorship of the Gospel of Mark."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7edffc2-c884-4d62-b757-d0cc02c19985",
                                                "sense_id": "6c666eb0-672e-3138-85af-ec75cb8ecf52",
                                                "text": "And Barnabas was determined to take with them John, whose surname was Mark. But Paul thought it not good to take him with them, who departed from them in Pamphylia, and went not with them to the work. And the contention was so sharp between them, that they departed asunder from the other; and so Barnabas took Mark, and sailed to Cyprus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f24af03e-684f-3641-80a4-070b0bb0203e",
                                        "entry_id": "8113bd45-ce91-3af7-8c28-a2eaaf16da85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Gospel of St. Mark, a book of the New Testament of the Bible. Traditionally the second of the four gospels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7a7d564-4c54-39d2-8f72-c79d14df13d0",
                                        "entry_id": "8113bd45-ce91-3af7-8c28-a2eaaf16da85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A village and civil parish in Somerset, England, previously in Sedgemoor district (OS grid ref ST3747)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
